        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://lakesnwoods.com/Jordan.htm",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first sawmill, called Holmes Mill, sparked the settlement that later became Jordan City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1872, the neighboring settlement of Brentwood merged with Jordan, creating the village that would later become a city.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first church building in Jordan was erected on land donated by Thomas Holmes, the town’s early patriarch.",
